MOVE EVERYTHING INTO A VIRTUAL MACHINEE STRUCT
 - so builtin functions (map/fold/filter) can call back into the vm

MERGE CLOSURES AND BUILTINFUNCTIONS
 - so they're treated uniformly in map/fold/filter

PROPER ERRORS FOR COMPILATION
 - stringify forms, backtrace based on builder debug info + builder's ip (position)

EVAL BUGS
 - function definition behaves in really weird and buggy ways
  -> propagating a closure from the subprogram to the enclosing program should be an error
  -> copy over function protos into the enclosing program?
   - needs to be Rc<>d

 - new globals aren't propagated into the enclosing program
  -> trivial fix
  -> as long as you don't want to allow sharing closures

SETTLE ON LIMITED EVAL?
 - explicit environment pass
 - keeps things simple
 - we're not a real lisp...

CLEAN UP POST-EVAL
 - don't emit the enclosing unused chunk
 - get data (like chunks) from the enclosing programbuilder
  -> we no longer need a separate finish() + Box<[Chunk]>, for example

STORE INTERNED SYMBOL INDEX IN SYMBOL VALUES
 - same logic as keywords
 - should work, right?

ALLOW BUILTIN FUNCTIONS TO CALL BACK INTO THE VIRTUAL MACHINE
 - explicit VirtualMachine struct passed around in run_chunk and to builtin fns
 - explicit call() function in program for calling closures
 - needs a bit of refactoring and work

FEATURES TO ADD BEFORE 1.0
 - explicit ValueType, (type x) built-in and better errors for builtin function readers
  -> maybe also use valuetype in addition / substraction errors
  
 - smaller instruction operand sizes - usize is HUGE
 - proper eval
 - proper list type
 - cleaner source code
 - macros!

DOCUMENT THE SELF CAPTURING CLOSURE LEAK
 - (set g (fn [] g)) leaks memory
 - but who would even do something like this???
 - swift apparently has this issue as well

NEW STANDARD FUNCTIONS
 - for/doseq
 - import
 - map/fold/filter
  -> operates over list, vector, string generically
  -> creates the same type of value for its result
 - read
 - cons, head (car), tail (cdr)
 - write
 - index (for vectors)
 - uneval: chunk -> source value dumping?
 - dec: (- x 1)
 - inc: (+ x 1)
 - zero?: (== 0)

NEW SPECIAl FORMS
 - and/or
 - (declare sym1 sym2 sym3...)

BUGS
 - recursion
  -> the Display implementation for containers can overflow the rust stack
  -> the default recursive Drop implementation for large tables also blows up the stack
  -> this is probably an issue in many places
  -> recheck em all
  -> using stacker at pain points seems to be the simplest solution

ERROR HANDLING
 - compile error backtraces
 - trace all debug info in the range for the IP for the frame instead of picking a single one

CLEANUPS
 - get rid of data_mut.push/pop, it's not clear
 - refactor code into smaller modules
 - decide on either ::from and such or .into()s
 - maybe switch run_chunk to chunk_index: usize based dispatch instead of &Chunk?

TODO READER SYNTAX
